# List what {{ record_id }} requires

`{{ record_id }}` ({{ kind | upper }}): {{ title }}

List every separate thing this record requires, one tenet each. Do not write, improve or review the record. Another writer will write a new record from your list alone and will never see the text below, so anything you leave out is lost and anything you add becomes a requirement.

## The record

{{ record_text }}
{% if original_text %}

## The record as its author first wrote it

Where the two texts disagree about what is required, this one decides.

{{ original_text }}
{% endif %}

## PRD clauses that govern it

{% for c in prd_clauses %}
- **{{ c.id }}** {{ c.text }}
{% endfor %}

## Rules

1. One tenet is one obligation: one thing a single test, command or file inspection could show to be true or false. A statement with a list gives one tenet per item. "A and B" gives two. A condition with its obligation ("when X, the server does Y") is one tenet; keep the condition in it.
2. Keep every obligation the record imposes. Do not add, drop, narrow, widen or strengthen one.
3. A reason or purpose is not a tenet. Put it under `rationale`.
4. Write each tenet in plain words and name every thing in full: no "it", "that type", "the above", "as follows".
5. Keep every name, number, path, command and code identifier exactly as the record has it, in backticks.
6. For each tenet give the PRD clauses it serves (`prd`), or an empty list. A tenet that contradicts a clause stays in `tenets` and is also listed under `conflicts`.
7. Under `terms`, list every project term a tenet uses with its meaning, taken from the record or the repository (`source`: the file and line). No meaning found: `"meaning": null`.
8. Under `must_not_say`, list what the clauses above forbid a record from saying, where this record could be tempted to say it.
{% if kind == "adr" %}

For an ADR, give each tenet a `part` in place of a modal: `decision` (what was decided), `problem` (the problem that forced a decision), `force` (a constraint that shaped it), `alternative` (an option considered, with why it was rejected), `benefit` or `cost` (a consequence).
{% else %}

Give each tenet the `modal` its statement carries: `MUST`, `MUST NOT` or `SHOULD`.
{% endif %}

## Return

One JSON object and nothing else:

    {"record_id": "{{ record_id }}",
     "tenets": [{"id": "T1", {% if kind == "adr" %}"part": "decision"{% else %}"modal": "MUST"{% endif %}, "text": "<one obligation in plain words>", "from": "<statement number or section>", "prd": ["<clause id>"]}],
     "rationale": ["<a reason the record gives>"],
     "terms": [{"name": "<term>", "meaning": "<meaning or null>", "source": "<file:line>"}],
     "must_not_say": ["<what a clause forbids>"],
     "conflicts": [{"tenet": "T1", "clause": "<clause id>", "why": "<how they disagree>"}]}
